# VIGIL standing twin — engagement config for vigil-twin.service.
# Copy to ~/.config/vigil/twin.env and edit. Leave VIGIL_TWIN_ARGS
# UNQUOTED as a whole (systemd word-splits it into separate CLI args).
#
# The refresh re-projects the SAME signed spine the world model is built
# from — `crucible twin refresh --once` reuses the attack-paths spine loader
# and the spine projector verbatim, writing ONE deterministic, advisory
# worldmodel snapshot (DIR/worldmodel-twin.json). It sends no traffic and
# reads only the local spine; the snapshot is never an oracle input.

# The writable engagement home (holds the signed spine + the twin snapshot
# output dir). This is the ONLY path the hardened unit is allowed to write
# (ReadWritePaths) besides its StateDirectory heartbeat dir.
VIGIL_BASE_DIR=%h/vigil/.vigil-live

# The refresh flags (spine + output dir, optional footholds). Example — project
# an engagement's worldmodel spine into a stored snapshot under the base dir:
VIGIL_TWIN_ARGS=--spine %h/vigil/.vigil-live/my-engagement/worldmodel-spine.json --out %h/vigil/.vigil-live/my-engagement/twin

# To ALSO compute an advisory attack-path report per foothold, append --source
# flags (repeatable). These reports are read-only + deterministic too:
# VIGIL_TWIN_ARGS=--spine %h/vigil/.vigil-live/my-engagement/worldmodel-spine.json --out %h/vigil/.vigil-live/my-engagement/twin --source host:foothold

# Determinism: do NOT pass --generated-at here unless you want a wallclock in the
# envelope — omitting it keeps the snapshot a pure, byte-identical function of the spine.
